[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977836203","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107574#issuecomment-2977836203","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107574","id":2977836203,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xfiyr","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T19:28:03Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T19:49:38Z","body":"> Not sure what's the point of adding `NSTask` implementation to the `execute`.\r\n\r\nI couldn't reliably build the Xcode project for iOS or visionOS with the previous implementation. It would regularly fail, as not all the output was captured. So the `** ARCHIVE SUCCEEDED **` text was missing and the subsequent steps failed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977836203/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977941174","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107574#issuecomment-2977941174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107574","id":2977941174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xf8a2","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T20:00:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T20:00:53Z","body":"> I couldn't reliably build the Xcode project for iOS or visionOS with the previous implementation.\r\n\r\nIf it's unreliable, the Unix implementation probably should be fixed (or replaced) instead. Is `execute_with_pipe` working better?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977941174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978197423","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107574#issuecomment-2978197423","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107574","id":2978197423,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xg6-v","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T21:24:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T21:25:55Z","body":"> If it's unreliable, the Unix implementation probably should be fixed (or replaced) instead. Is `execute_with_pipe` working better?\r\n\r\nI didn't try that, but it is quite different, as it relies on the caller to consume the data via the pipes.\r\n\r\nI refactored the UNIX implementation of `execute` to use `feof` and `fread` to read in chunks. Just like the prior implementation, the pipe returned by `popen` is returning an error at various stages of compilation:\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2025-06-17 at 07 20 42@2x](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7ce0a4b-33db-4858-a3d3-a1e9c96dc3bb)\r\n\r\nIn this example, you can see that it accumulated data up to `GatheringProvisioningInputs` before `f` returns an error. I think this is the same thing that is happening with `fgets`, which no doubt is checking for errors. \r\n\r\nI don't know why, but using `NSTask` reliably runs to completion. `popen` spawns the process using the default shell, and perhaps that is causing issues with `xcodebuild`, but that is pure speculation. In reality, I don't know _why_ `popen` is unreliable for xcodebuild.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978197423/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978268401","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107574#issuecomment-2978268401","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107574","id":2978268401,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xhMTx","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T21:50:33Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T21:50:33Z","body":"I've pushed \r\n\r\n* fix for device discovery, so it finds iPhones and iPads\r\n* Correctly read data from `NSTask`, regardless of data size.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2978268401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2982670897","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107574#issuecomment-2982670897","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107574","id":2982670897,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xx_Ix","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T04:46:54Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T04:46:54Z","body":"@bruvzg I've updated the PR as follows:\r\n\r\n- Removed the `OS_MacOS::execute` override using `NSTask`\r\n- Introduced an `_execute` method to `EditorExportPlatformAppleEmbedded` to use `execute_with_pipe`\r\n  - Now reliably executes build and deploys to physical device\r\n- Moved debugger issues to #107643\r\n\r\n## `execute_with_pipe` API\r\n\r\nThis API feels a bit clunky and needs some fixes / improvements:\r\n\r\n- Never cleans up old processes from the process map:\r\n\r\n  https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/24494d840e06402c26c03db36695b63c5322d624/drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp#L800-L803\r\n\r\n- Doesn't proved a way to wait for a process to complete (you must poll)\r\n\r\nFor 4.6, I think I'll submit a PR to improve `OS_Unix::execute` to use the same approach, rather than `popen`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2982670897/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2982684082","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107574#issuecomment-2982684082","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107574","id":2982684082,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xyCWy","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T04:56:00Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T04:56:00Z","body":"> Never cleans up old processes from the process map:\r\n\r\nNeither do `create_process`, it can be accessed by `is_process_running` and `get_process_exit_code` at any time, so I think keeping all process pids/exit codes is deliberate.\r\n\r\n> Doesn't proved a way to wait for a process to complete (you must poll)\r\n\r\nProbably should be a separate function similar to `is_process_running`, but blocking to work with both `execute_with_pipe` and `create_process`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2982684082/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2982743877","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107574#issuecomment-2982743877","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107574","id":2982743877,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xyQ9F","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin